{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "evidenceId": "2026-09-26-development-stabilization",
  "date": "2026-09-26",
  "subject": "Fresh-checkout harness repair and changed-runner development feedback",
  "claim": "The cache owner creates its ignored workspace directory on a fresh checkout. Product-acquisition-only edits select the cache owner. Four diagnostic cases cover valid limits and independent slot, bytecode-size and stack failures. Extracting return ownership classification lowers the current runner maximum from 2057 to 2028 total slots without raising limits. The changed runner compiles and packages on both hosts with retained tools, and the selected behaviors pass on Windows and Debian after correcting one test fixture.",
  "source": {
    "kind": "Other",
    "value": "Runner construction and initial behavior measurements used the worktree based on 6ab79a25aac7413fb6db4761f4740cb959f7c77f, including the pre-existing uncommitted collection/budget feature. Input hashes identify the measured files and products. The CI repair is committed as 0844170ca8e7db1f9ed46a92c1e915fc62d39404. The return-classification refactor and stack-witness correction remain with that pending feature work."
  },
